pe/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392709}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a33d5262-3afa-580b-b512-aba7c2576e69" :question/math-academy-id "q-50195" :question/problem "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2(x-1)?$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int (x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =2\\int (x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(x-1)^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-1,0,1.$\n\n![](images/92/92a2dbaa5726e6a1ab83fa879ad7b630b05e68a8e366db214b74d85269a849a9.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097303 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b595fdc-ac24-53b1-b485-072a76711f6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/83/83c166a9882661ec123b3f14bf76c9c7585052d0e85e24c4e41b7bbde4de9326.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330631} {:answer/id #uuid "71cb7ed8-c659-56d9-95c6-9bd73867660f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1e/1e746142e1dc26c247a6ac985c65072445658ad1f9b5ae298d246c1d81ab96bb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186330973} {:answer/id #uuid "7a615d72-2639-5796-9876-984ecf702dec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/56/566935c224696f817a798a9e0f608ba384b5da6af1f0bfec6ad769e910f1230c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331033} {:answer/id #uuid "8feb98b8-4798-558b-9d2a-1181de6e3f6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4b/4bcb4f24caba3010cb8bfffecacbd392ad5951d4e42873d467c9007ad2b7ea46.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331227} {:answer/id #uuid "a9f5ab31-edff-5dee-88f0-7ee4a29422a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1f/1fd9c2f2358171f102969930fde05347f50bd497f72