 y & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int (x+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(x+2)^{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-1,0,1.$\n\n![](images/2e/2ef13d3c7516974afcb94986ee9198b61d263f0ef53c344c02a5a8eb849e2c38.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386903 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cdbca57f-16aa-507a-9243-fc5de6668bda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4a/4acfee397d2c301aa7d005c8467319969bdfe1a487c284e51024a1851ef8a2e3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386905} {:answer/id #uuid "0e615e5e-edb5-5cf5-9379-57b9b7c05caa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0e/0e2d84423e017f6d126ef6b997a50d62a7de30f91c24aa64f2525ce4ae33cdd3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386906} {:answer/id #uuid "da6e7a98-d892-56d4-877b-036894b8ae90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/14/146aa5565c845f3fbfa66e6c215224236869199844cdbe51f2671c781b1c3705.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386907} {:answer/id #uuid "35676c31-bad6-527d-8d41-0491046fbe5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3e/3e93190f38d95bd30749fbd1342812c93f593a1d78243f810a3822d5d30eff82.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386908} {:answer/id #uuid "c70ce449-3435-5f49-bbc8-8c5d5d34005e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/55/557708220ba3876b0ae9dbf1d265d11e8d98cf1102ad084d93419543ede35c4b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da6e7a98-d892-56d4-877b-036894b8ae90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/14/146aa5565c845f3fbfa66e6c215224236869199844cdbe51f2671c781b1c3705.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386907} :answer-field/id #uuid "5dd2a4ff-6ada-5a27-9174-b3c1a697aa04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386904}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "06acaa38-08e2-563c-a31d-7a927dbf62a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-119139" :question/problem "Which of the following shows some of the solution curves of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-4{e}^{2x}?$" :question/worked-solution "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-4{e}^{2x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-4\\int {e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-4(\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}) \\\\  & =-2{e}^{2x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-2,0,2.$\n\n![](images/cc/cc2ee25a85be3ffdb055853f7665bd53d34003a74b96a14bb947bed39b18e83f.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386910 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "641c6f0c-3eaf-561b-8356-41cd00f60ef4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d5/d5f4f2b65878b9c152b5c87e1fac0473f0e76455fc5762ba10f21555d68a60c4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386912} {:answer/id #uuid "dc9f2778-f343-5bd4-8b1f-ffa35692fd8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3e/3e475d534a8f090caa9611d865e70a9717969ddc541c55d98200e19031bffe84.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386913} {:answer/id #uuid "21fe63ba-ca2a-5062-b8c9-c489ae9d0da5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a6/a65cbd746c3bb9abe495af168fd7c63e83ecf3d942c5fb478f3d7d312d140b4d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386914} {:answer/id #uuid "993af450-e9a5-57fb-a473-cf3bc2a14c65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/95/95b3d8fc43562341f93a2bccbcbe36d2a070a2dd6687606175ab5e9580f86e2f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386915} {:answer/id #uuid "6f16a9da-248f-5eb6-9d9c-67a9d932876b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0d/0d14e369d621a6c2d06b4db1485ff43f6af4be2014e9d26564c9ca1